# Commit and push

After any change to files in this repo, commit that change and push it to the tracked remote branch. Do this before you tell the user the task is done.

```text
# ❌ BAD — edit files, then stop
# leave the work uncommitted

# ✅ GOOD — same turn, after the edit
git add <the files you changed>
git commit
git push
```

- One commit per change. Message in English, about why.
- Push the current branch. Do not force-push.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, tokens, credentials).
- If the user says not to commit or not to push, skip it for that turn.
- If the hook rejects the commit, fix the problem and make a new commit. Do not amend unless the user asked.
